// Huffman coding - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# A Huffman code built for the ASCII of "Hello World!" alone. The code
# is only optimal for this one string, which is the whole limitation of
# single-table Huffman coding and the reason real formats store the table.
#   ' '   x1  -> 1110
#   '!'   x1  -> 100
#   'H'   x1  -> 1100
#   'W'   x1  -> 1111
#   'd'   x1  -> 001
#   'e'   x1  -> 1101
#   'r'   x1  -> 000
#   'o'   x2  -> 101
#   'l'   x3  -> 01
#
# encoded (37 bits, 96 raw):
# 1100110101011011110111110100001001100
